---
source: crates/mori-checker/src/tests.rs
description: "Code:\n\nprofile \"moriarty-beta/1\";\nagreement Header {\n  domain Preview = { id: \"preview\", chain: \"midnight\", network: \"preview\" };\n  domain Other = { id: \"other\", chain: \"midnight\", network: \"other\" };\n  asset USD = { domain: Preview, id: \"usd\", scale: 2, representation: \"native\" };\n  asset GOLD = { domain: Preview, id: \"gold\", scale: 3, representation: \"native\" };\n  account alice = { domain: Preview, id: \"alice\" };\n  account bob = { domain: Preview, id: \"bob\" };\n  account carol = { domain: Preview, id: \"carol\" };\n  intent pay = {\n    domain: Preview, asset: USD, signer: alice, key: \"k\", nonce: \"\", pre_head: \"h\",\n    valid: [0, 10],\n    gross_cap: 1 GOLD, fee_cap: 0 USD, net_floor: 1 USD,\n    operation: transfer(from: alice, to: bob, fee_to: carol, value: 1 USD, fee: 0 USD),\n    source_hash: \"s\", policy_digest: \"p\", failure: None,\n    observations: [\"price\"], disclosures: [], retained_effects: [], retained_duties: [],\n    delegation: SuccessOnly, recovery: None,\n  };\n}\n"
---
mori::check::empty_claim

  × The intent's `nonce` cannot be empty.
    ╭─[test.mori:11:66]
 10 │   intent pay = {
 11 │     domain: Preview, asset: USD, signer: alice, key: "k", nonce: "", pre_head: "h",
    ·                                                                  ─┬
    ·                                                                   ╰── empty
 12 │     valid: [0, 10],
    ╰────
  help: This value is part of what the owner signs, so it must be filled in.

mori::check::invalid_validity

  × A `transfer` or `repay` intent's `valid` must be a `rounds(...)` window.
    ╭─[test.mori:12:12]
 11 │     domain: Preview, asset: USD, signer: alice, key: "k", nonce: "", pre_head: "h",
 12 │     valid: [0, 10],
    ·            ───┬───
    ·               ╰── not a round window
 13 │     gross_cap: 1 GOLD, fee_cap: 0 USD, net_floor: 1 USD,
    ╰────
  help: For example:

            valid: rounds(domain: Preview, from: 0, to: 100),

mori::check::wrong_asset

  × `gross_cap` must be a `USD` amount because it is a cap on the intent's
  │ `asset`, but it is a `GOLD` amount.
    ╭─[test.mori:13:16]
 12 │     valid: [0, 10],
 13 │     gross_cap: 1 GOLD, fee_cap: 0 USD, net_floor: 1 USD,
    ·                ───┬──
    ·                   ╰── a `GOLD` amount
 14 │     operation: transfer(from: alice, to: bob, fee_to: carol, value: 1 USD, fee: 0 USD),
    ╰────

mori::check::s0_policy

  × A `transfer` or `repay` intent requires `failure: SuccessOnly`, but this
  │ is `None`.
    ╭─[test.mori:15:52]
 14 │     operation: transfer(from: alice, to: bob, fee_to: carol, value: 1 USD, fee: 0 USD),
 15 │     source_hash: "s", policy_digest: "p", failure: None,
    ·                                                    ──┬─
    ·                                                      ╰── must be `SuccessOnly`
 16 │     observations: ["price"], disclosures: [], retained_effects: [], retained_duties: [],
    ╰────
  help: Intents that run locally use the simplest policy: they succeed or fail
        as a whole, with nothing observed, disclosed, retained, delegated or
        recovered.

mori::check::s0_policy

  × A `transfer` or `repay` intent requires `observations: []`, but this is a
  │ list of 1 item.
    ╭─[test.mori:16:19]
 15 │     source_hash: "s", policy_digest: "p", failure: None,
 16 │     observations: ["price"], disclosures: [], retained_effects: [], retained_duties: [],
    ·                   ────┬────
    ·                       ╰── must be `[]`
 17 │     delegation: SuccessOnly, recovery: None,
    ╰────
  help: Intents that run locally use the simplest policy: they succeed or fail
        as a whole, with nothing observed, disclosed, retained, delegated or
        recovered.

mori::check::s0_policy

  × A `transfer` or `repay` intent requires `delegation: None`, but this is
  │ `SuccessOnly`.
    ╭─[test.mori:17:17]
 16 │     observations: ["price"], disclosures: [], retained_effects: [], retained_duties: [],
 17 │     delegation: SuccessOnly, recovery: None,
    ·                 ─────┬─────
    ·                      ╰── must be `None`
 18 │   };
    ╰────
  help: Intents that run locally use the simplest policy: they succeed or fail
        as a whole, with nothing observed, disclosed, retained, delegated or
        recovered.
